# SEO Guidelines

Keep the site discoverable and well-indexed. Apply these whenever you create or edit a `page.tsx` or `layout.tsx`.

## Metadata per page

Every route must export `metadata` (or `generateMetadata`) with a unique `title` and `description`. Don't rely only on the root layout.

```tsx
import type { Metadata } from 'next';

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: 'Historia | Iglesia Evangélica Antorcha de Cristo',
  description: 'Conoce la historia y los valores de nuestra iglesia en Tía Juana, Venezuela.',
  alternates: { canonical: '/history' },
  openGraph: {
    title: 'Historia | Iglesia Evangélica Antorcha de Cristo',
    description: 'Conoce la historia y los valores de nuestra iglesia.',
    type: 'website',
    locale: 'es_VE',
  },
};
```

- Title: ~60 chars max, descriptive, include the church name.
- Description: ~150-160 chars, in Spanish (the site is `lang="es"`).
- Set `metadataBase` once in the root layout so OG/canonical URLs resolve absolutely.

## Semantic & accessible HTML

- One `<h1>` per page; use `<h2>`/`<h3>` in order. Don't skip levels.
- Use landmarks: `<header>`, `<main>`, `<nav>`, `<footer>`, `<section>`.
- Every `<Image>` needs a meaningful `alt` (empty `alt=""` only for decorative images).

## Images & performance

- Always use `next/image`, set `width`/`height` or `fill`, and `priority` only for above-the-fold images.
- Prefer descriptive file names and modern formats.

## Links

- Use `next/link` for internal navigation (crawlable `<a href>`).
- External links: add `rel="noopener noreferrer"` (already done in social links).

## Don't

- ❌ Duplicate the same `title`/`description` across pages.
- ❌ Put primary content behind client-only rendering with no server HTML.
- ❌ Use `<div onClick>` for navigation instead of real links.
